RIP-IT! History File
$VER:RIP-IT!_V1.3

Version 0.1 -
          ->First test run on local BBS, VIP.
          ->Support for only 80 column screens.

Version 0.2 -
          ->Added 40 column support for all menu areas.

Version 1.0 -
          ->First Full public version. Fully tested
          ->Organized the whole thing into a more friendly format.

Version 1.1 - 25-FEB-95
    It's been a while since any updates and this is just a small one.
    FIXES:
          ->Corrected the program name in the log writes. It was writing
            Chemist II. This was because I stole some of my own code from
            my first ARexx program and did not catch all the changes:)
          ->Added the $VER: string to all programs and text files.
          ->Added some of the screens that I use to give you an idea of
            what is needed.
          ->Updated versions numbers.
          ->Updated History file;)
    BUGS:
          ->None known or reported at this time.

Version 1.2 - 13-APR-95 (Not Released)
          ->Oops! Left an old log call name in the NEWS file. Fixed.
          ->Updated versions numbers.
          ->Updated History file;)

Version 1.3 - 13-APR-95
          ->Added Get User to check the users 'Help Level'. The program
            will now exit if the users help level is NOT 0 'NOVICE'. This
            may be redundent, but some sysop's may install this program in
            the bbstext file where CNet might not know. Better safe I say;)
          ->Updated Doc's
          ->Updated versions numbers.
          ->Updated History file;)

Future: Create some more screens and include them in the archive.

